  "id": "DrugBank_DB08909 - MONDO_16601",
  "verbalization": "Glycerol Phenylbutyrate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Adult-onset Citrullinemia Type I through a shared pathway involving the urea cycle and phenylbutyric acid metabolism. The evidence suggests that Glycerol Phenylbutyrate is linked to Argininosuccinic Aciduria and Urea Cycle Disorder, both of which are associated with phenylbutyric acid accumulation. This accumulation is a key feature of Adult-onset Citrullinemia Type I, where the urea cycle is impaired, leading to the buildup of toxic byproducts. The indirect relationship between Glycerol Phenylbutyrate and the disease is mediated through its role in facilitating the metabolism of phenylbutyric acid, which is central to the disorder. The high confidence scores in the visible paths indicate a consistent and robust link, suggesting that Glycerol Phenylbutyrate may act as a potential therapeutic agent or a metabolic modifier in this condition.",
